        <h2>2. How to Use These Resources</h2>

        <p>
          Students can follow a simple learning process to make better use
          of the resources.
        </p>

        <h3>Step 1: Choose a Subject</h3>

        <p>
          Select the subject or career topic that you want to learn.
          For example, you can start with Java if you are learning
          programming.
        </p>

        <h3>Step 2: Learn the Basics</h3>

        <p>
          Read the basic concepts first. Understanding fundamentals makes
          advanced topics easier to learn.
        </p>

        <h3>Step 3: Practice</h3>

        <p>
          After learning a concept, practice examples and programming
          problems. Practice helps improve understanding and memory.
        </p>

        <h3>Step 4: Revise</h3>

        <p>
          Review important definitions, examples and questions regularly.
          Short revision sessions can help before examinations and interviews.
        </p>

        <h3>Step 5: Apply Your Knowledge</h3>

        <p>
          Try to use what you learn in projects, coding exercises,
          assignments or interview questions.
        </p>

        <div class="info-box">

          <strong>Simple learning method:</strong>

          <p>
            Learn → Understand → Practice → Revise → Apply
          </p>

        </div>

      </section>


