        <h2>4. DBMS Learning Resources</h2>

        <p>
          A Database Management System (DBMS) is software used to create,
          store, organize, manage and retrieve data efficiently.
        </p>

        <p>
          DBMS is an important subject for computer science students and is
          also commonly discussed in technical interviews.
        </p>

        <div class="resource-card">

          <h3>DBMS Basics</h3>

          <p>
            Learn databases, DBMS concepts, tables, keys, SQL,
            relationships, normalization and transactions.
          </p>

          <a href="dbms.html">
            Learn DBMS
          </a>

        </div>

        <h3>Important DBMS Topics</h3>

        <ul>
          <li>Database and DBMS</li>
          <li>Database Models</li>
          <li>Tables and Records</li>
          <li>Primary Key and Foreign Key</li>
          <li>SQL Commands</li>
          <li>CRUD Operations</li>
          <li>Relationships</li>
          <li>Normalization</li>
          <li>Transactions</li>
          <li>ACID Properties</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="info-box">

          <strong>Study Tip:</strong>

          <p>
            Practice SQL queries along with the theory. Writing queries
            regularly makes database concepts easier to understand.
          </p>

        </div>

      </section>


      <!-- DATA STRUCTURES RESOURCE -->
