        <h2>5. Data Structures Learning Resources</h2>

        <p>
          Data structures are methods of organizing and storing data so that
          it can be accessed and processed efficiently.
        </p>

        <p>
          Learning data structures helps students improve programming,
          problem-solving and technical interview skills.
        </p>

        <div class="resource-card">

          <h3>Data Structures Basics</h3>

          <p>
            Learn arrays, linked lists, stacks, queues, trees, heaps,
            hashing, graphs, searching and sorting.
          </p>

          <a href="data-structures.html">
            Learn Data Structures
          </a>

        </div>

        <h3>Important Data Structure Topics</h3>

        <ul>
          <li>Arrays</li>
          <li>Linked Lists</li>
          <li>Stacks</li>
          <li>Queues</li>
          <li>Trees</li>
          <li>Heaps</li>
          <li>Hashing</li>
          <li>Graphs</li>
          <li>Searching Algorithms</li>
          <li>Sorting Algorithms</li>
          <li>Time Complexity</li>
          <li>Space Complexity</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Why Learn Data Structures?</h3>

        <p>
          Data structures help students write efficient programs and
          understand how data is stored, searched and processed.
          They are also useful for coding tests and technical interviews.
        </p>

      </section>
          <!-- DIGITAL LOGIC RESOURCE -->
