        <h2>6. Digital Logic Learning Resources</h2>

        <p>
          Digital Logic Design is an important foundation of computer
          science and computer engineering. It explains how digital
          systems represent, process and store information.
        </p>

        <p>
          Students can learn number systems, logic gates, Boolean algebra,
          truth tables, K-maps and digital circuits step by step.
        </p>

        <div class="resource-card">

          <h3>Digital Logic Basics</h3>

          <p>
            Learn number systems, logic gates, Boolean algebra,
            K-maps, combinational circuits and sequential circuits.
          </p>

          <a href="digital-logic.html">
            Learn Digital Logic
          </a>

        </div>

        <h3>Important Topics</h3>

        <ul>
          <li>Number Systems</li>
          <li>Binary Conversion</li>
          <li>Logic Gates</li>
          <li>Boolean Algebra</li>
          <li>Truth Tables</li>
          <li>K-Maps</li>
          <li>Half Adder and Full Adder</li>
          <li>Multiplexers and Demultiplexers</li>
          <li>Encoders and Decoders</li>
          <li>Flip-Flops</li>
          <li>Registers</li>
          <li>Counters</li>
        </ul>

      </section>


