      <!-- STUDY TIPS -->
      <section class="content-section" id="study-tips">

        <h2>9. Study Tips for Students</h2>

        <p>
          Good study habits can make learning more effective and help
          students manage academic and career preparation together.
        </p>

        <h3>1. Create a Study Schedule</h3>

        <p>
          Plan your study time and divide larger topics into smaller
          sections. A simple schedule can help you stay consistent.
        </p>

        <h3>2. Understand Before Memorizing</h3>

        <p>
          Try to understand the meaning of a concept before memorizing
          definitions or answers.
        </p>

        <h3>3. Practice Regularly</h3>

        <p>
          Practice coding problems, SQL queries, numerical questions
          and important exam questions regularly.
        </p>

        <h3>4. Make Short Notes</h3>

        <p>
          Write important formulas, definitions, examples and key points
          in your own words for quick revision.
        </p>

        <h3>5. Revise Frequently</h3>

        <p>
          Regular revision helps you remember concepts for a longer time
          and makes examination preparation easier.
        </p>

        <h3>6. Work on Communication</h3>

        <p>
          Students preparing for placements should also practice speaking,
          explaining technical concepts and answering interview questions.
        </p>

        <div class="info-box">

          <strong>Simple Study Routine:</strong>

          <p>
            Learn a concept → Practice it → Make notes → Revise it →
            Test yourself.
          </p>

        </div>

