      <!-- FAQ -->
      <section class="content-section" id="faq">

        <h2>10. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <h3>1. Are the Learnix resources useful for beginners?</h3>

        <p>
          Yes. The resources are written in simple language and introduce
          important concepts step by step.
        </p>

        <h3>2. What subjects are available?</h3>

        <p>
          Learnix currently provides resources covering Java, DBMS,
          Data Structures, Digital Logic, placement preparation and
          resume preparation.
        </p>

        <h3>3. Can I use these resources for exam preparation?</h3>

        <p>
          Yes. Students can use the explanations, examples and topic
          lists for learning and revision before examinations.
        </p>

        <h3>4. Can beginners learn Java from Learnix?</h3>

        <p>
          Yes. The Java resource starts with basic programming concepts
          and gradually introduces important object-oriented programming
          topics.
        </p>

        <h3>5. Why are Data Structures important?</h3>

        <p>
          Data Structures help students understand how data can be
          organized and processed efficiently. They are also useful
          for coding tests and technical interviews.
        </p>

        <h3>6. Is DBMS useful for placements?</h3>

        <p>
          Yes. Database concepts and SQL are commonly useful in software
          development and technical interview preparation.
        </p>

        <h3>7. What should I study for placements?</h3>

        <p>
          Students can prepare aptitude, logical reasoning, verbal ability,
          coding, technical subjects, communication skills and interview
          questions.
        </p>

        <h3>8. Why is resume preparation important?</h3>

        <p>
          A resume presents your education, skills, projects and experience
          to employers. A clear resume can make it easier for recruiters
          to understand your profile.
        </p>

        <h3>9. How often should I study?</h3>

        <p>
          Consistent daily study is generally more effective than studying
          only immediately before an examination or interview.
        </p>

        <h3>10. Can I use Learnix resources for self-learning?</h3>

        <p>
          Yes. Students can use the resources as a starting point for
          learning concepts, practicing and revising important topics.
        </p>

